job.description:
Are you a Junior Requirement Engineer who would like to apply their experience to the competitive space industry, requiring the highest level of international security and contributing to Galileo and IRIS2, Europe's satellite navigation systems?  

Please note: Due to mandatory security clearance requirements, only EU nationals are eligible for this position.  

**Your role in our team**  
CGI Space Netherlands is looking for an engineer to work at our client site in France (Paris area). The objective of the job is to provide system requirement engineering for several space programs. You will contribute to the definition, analysis, documentation, and management of requirements across the different satellite projects of the EU.  

This is a junior-level position intended for engineers with 2.5–5 years of experience, ideally with a background in aerospace, (software) engineering or database management.  

Activities to be performed are (but not limited to):  


* Requirement Elicitation: Refining and iterating on the existing requirement documents and their traceability and architecture.
* Requirement Documentation: Writing clear, testable and traceable system and subsystem requirements.
* Traceability management: Importing and structuring security requirements in IBM DOORS and managing their traceability and architecture.
* Change control: Handle updates and changes to requirements, assess impact, and manage the baseline.
* Improvement advice: Provide advice on evolutions of requirements needed to improve various systems, also considering lessons learnt.


**How you strengthen our team**  
This is you:  


* Good client facing skills / Interpersonal skills;
* English speaking and writing skills;
* EU passport; Please note that holding an EU passport is mandatory for obtaining an EU Personal Security Clearance, which is part of our selection process.
* Experience in aerospace, (software) engineering or database management (minimal 2,5 years);
* Able and willing to apply for a personal security clearance.


Things that are nice to have:  


* Experience in requirement management;
* Experience in using requirements tooling, such as DOORS or similar tooling;
* Experience in the security domain.


**Where will you be working?**  
You will join CGI Space Netherlands and work at our client site in France, in the Paris area. You will contribute to several European space programmes, including Galileo and IRIS2, and work in an international environment where system requirements, security and satellite technology come together.  

**AI & Futureproof**  
At CGI, we continuously assess the impact of new technologies on our services and the solutions we develop for our clients. Developments in AI and automation are also playing an increasingly important role.  

**Why CGI?**  
CGI is one of the world's largest IT consulting companies. Our people help keep the Netherlands running. Government institutions, banks, aerospace organizations, infrastructure providers, and companies in the energy, transport and manufacturing sectors are all clients of CGI. We work on meaningful projects that impact the daily lives of millions of people. We combine a strong local presence with global expertise, our ecosystem and colleagues around the world.  

We are proud of the impactful projects we deliver together with our colleagues and clients.  

At CGI, we highly value diversity and inclusion because it not only strengthens collaboration but often leads to better results. We look forward to your contribution to our team. You will work in small, self-managing teams consisting of experts in your field.  

At CGI, we combine challenging projects with excellent employment conditions:  


* A permanent employment contract from day one;
* A competitive salary aligned with your experience and seniority;
* 8.33% holiday allowance;
* Bonus and profit-sharing scheme;
* 20 statutory and 5 additional vacation days (based on full-time employment);
* Lease car budget / mobility budget;
* NS Business Card;
* Annual training budget and access to the CGI Academy;
* Bicycle scheme through CGI;
* The opportunity to invest up to 3% of your salary in CGI shares, with CGI matching your investment;
* An allowance when participating in CGI’s collective health insurance plan;
* €40 net monthly home working allowance;
* Excellent pension scheme;
* Hybrid working.


**Join our team of experts and apply today!**  
We will contact you as soon as possible. If you have any questions about the position, please contact Director Consulting Services Jeroen Meulman via jeroen.meulman@cgi.com or +31 6 53930249.  

Questions about the recruitment process? Please contact Recruitment Business Partner Ferhun Dogan via ferhun.dogan@cgi.com or +31 6 11484743.  

**We do not work with external recruitment agencies. Therefore, unsolicited acquisition is not appreciated.**  

